ie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T19:58:07Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T19:59:06Z","body":"A13 is an Apple 6 GPU – and you are running iOS 18, so there should be no reason that transparent black isn't supported. I can't find any other evidence of this error using searching with Google or across GitHub repos.\n\nSampler border colour is not listed in [Apple's Metal Feature Tables](https://developer.apple.com/metal/Metal-Feature-Set-Tables.pdf) as having limited device / GPU support, so I'm going with a bug in the validation layer. \n\nIf you disable validation, does the app work normally without visual artefacts?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3873529977/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3874507461","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116090#issuecomment-3874507461","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116090","id":3874507461,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7m8ErF","user":{"login":"cpl-s-matsuyama","id":26297239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2Mjk3MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26297239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpl-s-matsuyama","html_url":"https://github.com/cpl-s-matsuyama","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpl-s-matsuyama/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpl-s-matsuyama/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpl-s-matsuyama/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpl-s-matsuyama/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpl-s-matsuyama/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpl-s-matsuyama/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpl-s-matsuyama/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpl-s-matsuyama/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpl-s-matsuyama/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T23:51:57Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T23:51:57Z","body":"> Are you using shader baking, and if yes, does it work with shader baking disabled?\n\nI am not using Shader Baking. The validation error occurs without it.\n\n> If you disable validation, does the app work normally without visual artefacts?\n\nWhen Metal API Validation is disabled (i.e., running the exported application rather than debugging through Xcode), it works without any issues.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3874507461/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3874510039","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116090#issuecomment-3874510039","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116090","id":3874510039,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7m8FTX","user":{"login":"cpl-s-matsuyama","id":26297239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2Mjk3MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26297239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpl-s-matsuyama","html_url":"https://github.com/cpl-s-matsuyama","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpl-s-matsuyama/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpl-s-matsuyama/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpl-s-matsuyama/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpl-s-matsuyama/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpl-s-matsuyama/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpl-s-matsuyama/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpl-s-matsuyama/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpl-s-matsuyama/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cpl-s-matsuyama/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T23:52:51Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T23:52:51Z","body":"According to Apple's Metal Feature Tables, the \"Border Color\" feature appears to be limited to Metal 3 and later. Could this be what \"Sampler border color\" refers to?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3874510039/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3874628401","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116090#issuecomment-3874628401","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116090","id":3874628401,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7m8iMx","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T00:27:30Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T00:27:30Z","body":"> According to Apple's Metal Feature Tables, the \"Border Color\" feature appears to be limited to Metal 3 and later. Could this be what \"Sampler border color\" refers to?\n\nI think you are right, and I searched for sampler + border + color, so I didn't find it. Incidentally, this code behaviour hasn't changed since the original release, so perhaps Apple's validation layer was updated to check this.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3874628401/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3874766314","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116090#issuecomment-3874766314","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116090","id":3874766314,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7m9D3q","user":{"lo